              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Malayalam for a holiday, then the Malayalam for I'll call."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: വീട്",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "വീട് (vīṭŭ) — \"a house\", and also \"home\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "എന്റെ വീട് (enṟe vīṭŭ) — \"my house\", with എന്റെ, \"my\", which you already know."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "വീട് (vīṭŭ) is native Dravidian: DEDR 5393 lists it, \"house\", under the verb \"to let go, leave off\", with Tamil viṭu. DEDR 5393 notes Sanskrit avamocana, \"inn\", as a translation of Tamil viṭuti."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The place every visit starts."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
